course: dictionary
lesson: 2946
title: Comparing with drier
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Drier is the comparison form of dry. Dry, drier, driest works like small, smaller, smallest: the -er ending compares two things. «Deserts are drier than rainforests» means deserts have less water or wetness than rainforests.
explain: Drier can also be a noun, a machine that dries things. Some people spell it dryer. «Put the wet towels in the dryer» means put them in the machine that dries them. Look at the words around drier to see whether it is describing something or naming a machine.
explain: Context gives clues. «Hotter, drier years make bushfire seasons longer and fiercer.» The word hotter tells you the years are getting warmer, so drier must be about less rain or water. Test it: swap in less wet and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Drier is the comparative of dry: it compares two things and shows one has less water or wetness.
fact: A drier (also spelled dryer) is a machine that dries things, such as a clothes dryer or a hair dryer.
fact: «Trees release so much water from their leaves» that the Amazon makes much of its own rain, so cutting down the forest can make the region drier.
fact: Phrases to know: drier than, a tumble dryer, a hair dryer.
fact: Scientists use drier in science and geography, for example when they compare deserts with rainforests.
exercise: «Deserts are drier than rainforests.» What does drier mean here? | Hotter and brighter than | Softer and warmer than | Having more rain than | *Having less water or wetness than
exercise: Which word names the machine that dries wet clothes? | Damp | *Drier | Drizzle | Drought
exercise: Which word in «Hotter, drier years make bushfire seasons longer» is the comparative of dry? | Seasons | Years | *Drier | Hotter
test: «Cutting down the forest can make the region drier.» Drier here means: | Bigger and taller | Greener and brighter | *Having less water or wetness | More rainy
test: Which word is another spelling of the machine drier? | Dyer | Dire | Drear | *Dryer
exam: Which word means a machine that dries things? | Drought | Drizzle | *Dryer | Dry
